Blatant spoilers re: cursing a bag of holding

I didn't see this question adequately answered, so I'll explain in 
detail why and how someone would want to curse a bag of holding:
 
A bag of holding allows you to carry objects at 1/2 of their 
weight, I believe.  (Don't quote me on this.)  A blessed bag of 
holding allows one to carry stuff at even less weight.  The problem 
is, if one has a full bag of holding, and blessed it, the program 
still seems to think you're carrying the same amount of weight, 
when in fact it should be considerably less.  So even if you take 
all the things out of the bag and drop them (and the bag, even), 
you should end up with less carrying capacity, since as you remove 
items from the bag, the program only subtracts the weight of what 
it thinks it added in the first place.  Yich.
 
I'm not entirely sure about how Nethack handles weights, so you 
might end up being able to reset your weight somehow.  I'm guessing 
that that doesn't happen anywhere, just as a hunch.
 
You can utilize this bug, if ye are one of little morals (as if I'm 
not planning to do it as soon as I find myself with a bag of 
holding and about three potions of water), by cursing a bag of 
holding.  Now the program will deduct more weight for items when 
you take them out than it added when you put them in, so you end up 
being able to carry more.  Of course, your items aren't safe in a 
cursed bag of holding, so the best way to handle this is to:
 
1. Bless an empty bag of holding.
2. Pick up the bag, two potions of water and as many rocks as you 
   can carry.
3. Put rocks in bag.  Pick up more rocks.  Repeat #3 until you can't
   carry a single rock more.
4. Make the two potions of water into holy water and curse the bag 
   of holding.
5. Drop the bag.  (I believe items evaporate when you remove 
   them then from a cursed bag of holding, but dropping it should 
   be simplest.)
   
You should be able to carry, what, about twice as much in the 
future.

